<%#
  The bookend to the header, and the answer to "what exactly am I looking at?"
  — asked most often of an instance somebody else deployed.

  Two numbers, not one, and they answer different questions (docs/deploy.md):
  the version is the release you can say out loud, the revision is the commit
  that is actually running. A version alone cannot tell you whether the deploy
  you just did took. The revision links to the commit, because a bare hex
  string with no way to look it up is half a fact.

  Outside a container with no VERSION file and outside development, the
  revision is "unknown" — there is nothing to link to, so it is left out
  entirely rather than shown as a word that looks like a value.
%>
<footer class="px-14 py-5 border-t border-rule">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-xs text-faint">
    <span>
      Spool
      <%= link_to "v#{Spool::VERSION}", "#{Spool::SOURCE_URL}/releases/tag/v#{Spool::VERSION}",
            class: "font-mono hover:text-ink" %>
    </span>

    <% if (revision = Rails.application.config.x.revision) != "unknown" %>
      <span class="w-px h-3 bg-rule"></span>
      <%= link_to revision, "#{Spool::SOURCE_URL}/commit/#{revision}",
            class: "font-mono hover:text-ink" %>
    <% end %>

    <span class="w-px h-3 bg-rule"></span>
    <span>Rails <span class="font-mono"><%= Rails.version %></span></span>

    <span class="w-px h-3 bg-rule"></span>
    <span>Ruby <span class="font-mono"><%= RUBY_VERSION %></span></span>

    <%= link_to "GitHub", Spool::SOURCE_URL, class: "ml-auto hover:text-ink" %>
  </div>
</footer>
